  "$verifiersComment": "Independent readers for the verification stage (§10.1). Every entry is not_implemented: none is written. They are registered rather than omitted so that a result may reference a known id, while a capability claiming `independent_reader_available` still has to name a verifier whose status is `implemented` — which none is. Registering an id is not claiming it works.",
  "$detectorsComment": "Each detector declares whether it exists. Nothing does: the registry describes the taxonomy the adapters will implement, and publishing it as current capability would tell consumers this build can inspect PDFs. `implemented` requires an `adapter` module that really exists, so the status cannot be advanced by editing a string.",
  "parsers": {
    "pdf.parser": {
      "mediaTypes": [
        "application/pdf"
      ],
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "not_implemented",
      "waitingOn": "#4"
    },
    "image.png_parser": {
